The legal texts come from SeyLII, Seychelles Legal Information Institute (Laws.Africa Peachjam platform, read through the Internet Archive):

  SeyLII, https://seylii.org, point-in-time versions of each act, read from archived copies of its
  pages on the Internet Archive (https://web.archive.org), retrieved 2026-10-28.

Licence and terms, as SeyLII states them: CC BY-NC 4.0, crediting SeyLII as the source (SeyLII terms of use, s. 9, archived https://web.archive.org/web/20260301144011id_/https://seylii.org/terms-of-use/).
CC BY-NC 4.0: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/legalcode

Attribution:

  Source: SeyLII (https://seylii.org), licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International licence (CC BY-NC 4.0).

The texts may be used only for non-commercial purposes. This repository is private; whether and how it
may be published is the owner's decision under these terms.

Changes made by Lexifina: each version was converted to one Markdown file per provision, one paragraph per
line; spacing, quotes and dashes were normalised; editorial notes, Part and Chapter headings were left out;
and the versions were arranged as git commits credited to the laws SeyLII names for each change.
The wording of the law was not changed. Neither SeyLII nor Laws.Africa endorses this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the
tools) are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
